    "q-42711": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42711",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$0.5-4.5=$",
      "worked_solution": "To subtract $4.5$ from $0.5,$ we break up $4.5$ into its whole number part ($4$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- We start at $0.5$ on the number line and move $4$ places to the left, which brings us to $-3.5.$\n\n- Then, we move $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $-4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149078/assets/10fd02636a2fde424ef1b176b1e204a8b436c4500acc09759f488d7efc5cbefc.png)\n\nThis gives $0.5-4.5=-4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
